  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-10-25 (dev 2399d5ad7c; owner-requested re-check of the 17 actionable open P2 violated INV/META items; fixtures archived under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/premise_check_10252026/). VERDICT: STALE-TEXT; still violated. Fake scip-python / rust-analyzer first on PATH (log argv, write no index): (a) a fixture with .hypergumbo.toml [backends] scip_python = true and no flag or env -> `hypergumbo run` launched `scip-python --version` then `index --cwd <fixture> --project-name fxpy --project-version 0 --output /tmp/hypergumbo-scip-python-XXXX/index.scip` -- the analysed repository switches the launch on for itself; (b) a Cargo fixture with HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1, empty XDG_STATE_HOME, NO trust grant -> `rust-analyzer scip <fixture>` (runs build.rs). invoke.py:103 and :149 both `run = runner if runner is not None else subprocess.run`; scip_python analyzer.py:109 raw tempfile.TemporaryDirectory; safety_zones.py has no backend wrapper. MISSTATED: 'after a trust-backend grant' -- flag, env and grant are ALTERNATIVE enablers (backend_selection.py:241-253); the env var alone launched it. UNDER-SCOPED: the enumeration omits the scip-python --version probe (repo_inspect_probe, scip_python_install.py:56). Drift: the scip-python argv is now `index --cwd ... --output <tmp>/index.scip` (WI-nijod, 1d26944212); io-allowlist.yaml:654 target still has the old form. NOT checked: verify-claims self-proof, a real backend run."  # c432
