  message: "Satisfied. Merged as PR #1856 (dev 65124fe5ac). safety_zones gains backend_index_scip_python and backend_index_rust_analyzer (zone analyser_backend, declared in docs/hypergumbo-self-catalog/analyser_backend_sinks.yaml and loaded by the claims file); both invoke modules default to them; the scip-python scratch dir is safety_zones.tmp_artifact_dir; runtime-cli-no-subprocess now enumerates both launches with their enablers (flag, env var, or trust grant / config tier -- alternatives) plus the scip-python --version probe; SECURITY.md regenerated; the three findings left the I/O allowlist (check-io-allowlist OK, 263 sites). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE on merged dev, the premise check's own repro re-run with fake scip-python / rust-analyzer first on PATH and a spy on the production module attribute: (a) the fixture whose .hypergumbo.toml sets [backends] scip_python = true, `hypergumbo run` -> zone wrapper calls [backend_index_scip_python scip-python index], and the fake binary logged `scip-python index --cwd <fixture> ... --output /tmp/hypergumbo-scip-python-*/index.scip`; (b) the Cargo fixture with HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1 and no trust grant -> [backend_index_rust_analyzer rust-analyzer scip], binary logged `rust-analyzer scip <fixture>`. Every launch reached its declared wrapper. check-self-claims: 18 claims unchanged (18 confirmed_with_caveats). NOT checked: a real backend run (no real binaries used), and whether any claim should PROHIBIT the analyser_backend zone (none does; the zone is declared and enumerated, not forbidden)."  # ab63
